<span class="c">#include "DemoCommon.xcconfig"</span>
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p>OK. After <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">pod install</code>, the warning is gone.</p>

<h4 id="points-to-note-about-xcconfig-inheritance">Points to Note About xcconfig Inheritance</h4>

<p>Here I added a common DemoCommon.xcconfig configuration, to export common macro variables.</p>

<p><img src="/assets/images/20201004XcodeBuildXcconfigFile/xcconfig7.avif" alt="xcconfig" /></p>

<p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS</code> means inheriting the common environment variables and adding them to preprocessing — that is, adding this line so that the related macro definitions can be referenced in code.</p>

<div class="language-sh highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><!-- <td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
</pre></td> --><td class="rouge-code"><pre>GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS <span class="o">=</span> <span class="si">$(</span>inherited<span class="si">)</span> <span class="nv">SUNYAZHOU_COM</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s1">'$(SUNYAZHOU_COM)'</span> <span class="nv">SYZ_TEST</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s1">'$(SYZ_TEST)'</span> 
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>

<p>Note the format when there are multiple variables:</p>

<div class="language-sh highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><!-- <td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
</pre></td> --><td class="rouge-code"><pre> GCC_PREPROCESSOR_DEFINITIONS <span class="o">=</span> <span class="si">$(</span>inherited<span class="si">)</span>空格<span class="o">(</span>不能加换行<span class="o">)</span>+SUNYAZHOU_COM<span class="o">=</span><span class="s1">'$(SUNYAZHOU_COM)'</span>+空格<span class="o">(</span>不能加换行<span class="o">)</span><span class="nv">SYZ_TEST</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s1">'$(SYZ_TEST)'</span> 
</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>
<p>The pitfall I hit here was adding 20+ variables and writing a big pile of them. In the end, unless the format matched the above, the build failed and the variables couldn’t be found.</p>

